# `node_modules` (593 MB) and `.next` (343 MB) are both rebuilt inside the
# image — `npm ci` installs the first from the lockfile and `next dev`
# generates the second — so copying them in only slows the build down, and a
# host `node_modules` built on a different platform can be actively wrong.
#
# Both are also masked by anonymous volumes in docker-compose.yml, so the
# container's own copies survive the source bind mount.
node_modules
.next
out

.env*.local
.git
npm-debug.log*
